---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-privy';
const title = 'Yotpo Email & SMS vs Privy for Shopify: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Yotpo Email & SMS is retired. Choose capture and messaging ownership without arbitrary graduation thresholds.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I choose Yotpo Email & SMS today?",
    "answer": "Yotpo states that the application is decommissioned. This is now a migration decision, separate from retaining its Reviews or Loyalty products."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is there an order-count limit for using Privy?",
    "answer": "This comparison establishes no universal graduation threshold. Assess the specific journeys, data and operating requirements your store needs."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can Privy remain the popup tool?",
    "answer": "Yes, that is a role to evaluate. Confirm the destination integration and signup metadata, and assign a single owner for the welcome incentive and subsequent messages."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I replace Yotpo Reviews too?",
    "answer": "That is a separate decision from replacing retired Email & SMS. Inventory review display, invitations and any required data before changing those services."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I export from the retired account now?",
    "answer": "Do not assume access remains available. Use records already retained and ask the relevant support teams about missing data; this page promises no recovery or export access."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I also evaluate Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "You can include Sequenzy in the email shortlist. Verify the required Shopify events, suppression, consent handling and current commercial terms before choosing it; it is not assumed to replace SMS or review infrastructure."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-cyan-100/90">/</span>
        <span class="text-cyan-100/90">Yotpo Email & SMS vs Privy</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="badge">Migration comparison · reviewed November 24, 2026</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Yotpo Email &amp; SMS vs Privy for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Choose capture and messaging ownership without arbitrary graduation thresholds. Yotpo confirms that Email &amp; SMS has been decommissioned. This page evaluates a replacement workflow, not a trial of two currently available senders.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Privy is more than a popup collector</h2>
        <p>The current Shopify listing describes popups, email, SMS and automation. The old claim that Privy is only suitable below a fixed order count is unsupported. Evaluate the workflows your store needs, including branching, purchase exits and support ownership, rather than declaring it inadequate at a revenue or capture-rate threshold.</p>
        <h2>Choose between one sender and a capture-only role</h2>
        <p>Privy can be assessed for both capture and messaging, or for capture alongside another chosen sender. Write the ownership map first: form submission, discount delivery, welcome, cart, post-purchase and winback. If another service owns welcome, disable the competing welcome path only after verifying the new one; two active senders can issue different offers to the same signup.</p>
        <h2>Proposed print-on-demand signup scenario</h2>
        <p>For a hypothetical apparel store, submit a design-interest form as a new contact, an existing subscriber and a previous customer. Check that the promised incentive arrives once, that collection interest reaches the intended branch, and that a purchase stops the planned cart reminder. These are proposed checks, not a claimed popup conversion experiment.</p>
        <h2>Measure the handoff rather than capture rate alone</h2>
        <p>Record form submission, accepted subscription, delivery and first purchase as distinct steps. A popup that collects more addresses can still send poor-fit traffic into a welcome series or create repeat coupon requests. Compare sources and offers before attributing a change to the app; no universal capture percentage establishes that a store must buy Privy.</p>
        <h2>Retained reviews do not determine the email sender</h2>
        <p>A skincare store can keep its review infrastructure while replacing the retired Yotpo messaging product. Establish who sends the invitation and how customer support or a return affects follow-up. Do not assume Privy has every review field you need, or that buying a broader suite is required merely to display existing reviews.</p>
        <h2>Evaluate operating fit with real requirements</h2>
        <p>List the post-purchase education, cart exclusions and winback branches you actually plan to operate, then inspect whether the chosen configuration supports each. Obtain a current quote using the provider’s billing definitions, planned contact volume and channel usage. Remove unused overlapping subscriptions only after the handoff is confirmed; neither low order value nor high traffic proves which stack costs less.</p>
        <h2>Where Sequenzy fits</h2>
        <p>If you are considering Sequenzy for email, compare the same required events, exclusions and operating tasks before selecting it. Confirm current Shopify integration scope and pricing directly. Do not assume it replaces the SMS sender, review collection or loyalty service.</p>
        <h2>Primary evidence and limits</h2>
        <p>Supplier documentation checked November 24, 2026. No live migration, deliverability experiment or merchant revenue test was performed. Current account eligibility, quotes and missing historical records remain to be confirmed.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo decommissioning notice</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/privy">Privy current Shopify listing</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-privy">Omnisend vs Privy</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-privy">Sequenzy vs Privy</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend">Yotpo vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/print-on-demand">Email apps for print-on-demand</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/welcome-series">Welcome series playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Yotpo Email &amp; SMS vs Privy FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
